💡 **SUGGESTION: this block near-duplicates `_capResumedContext`'s trim block**

This ~28-line sequence — capture `_liveRequestTokens()`, call `localTrimValve` with the same argument shape (`messages` / `window` / `settings` / `overheadTokens` from `estimateRequestTokens`), assign `_agent.state.messages` + `_persistedCount`, `_logDiagnostic('… tokens=$tokens -> $after (dropped …)')`, dim `[context trimmed] …` note — is a near-copy of the resume boot cap's block in `_capResumedContext` (`agent_cli_compaction.dart:534-556`), which this PR's description itself calls "the same endpoint-free path the resume boot cap uses, gh-1425".

A small helper on `AgentCli` would keep the two call sites byte-consistent as the valve's contract evolves (the next caller — the checkpoint-restore guard — is already drifting toward a third copy):

```dart
/// Applies the mechanical local-trim valve to the live state and prints
/// the dim receipt. Returns the post-trim token estimate, or null when
/// the valve found nothing droppable.
Future<int?> _applyLocalTrim(String reason, String Function(int, int) note)
```

Not blocking — the duplication is small, both copies pass the same tests today — but it's the kind of divergence that bites when the marker text or `_persistedCount` rule changes in one copy only.
